{
  "_doc": "Stream E (M2). Radiant job frames (after Farhold data/job-frames.json). The job board fills each `needs` slot from what EXISTS right now in the zone copy (a frame whose slots cannot all bind is never offered, so nothing points at an empty field). Slot types: monster (a type from the zone's camps; `band: 'zone'` = level within the zone band; `family` filter), vignette, settlement (`same: 'giver'` = the giver's own), fort, farm (a farm placement; `from: 'farm.pests'` = one of that farm template's pests in data/provinces/sites.json), cave (a cave placement), rare (`alive` = currently spawned), dungeon. Text placeholders: {slot.name}, {slot.id}, {zone.name}, {giver.role}. Rewards follow the quest rule: xp = share of a level, gold = multiple of a kill's gold. Each frame has a `where` template (same placeholders) for the tracker/journal location line. ANGLER JOBS (play-test 5, T25): slot type `fish` = a fish from data/provinces/angling.json that lives in the giver's zone (bands overlap the zone band, `band: 'zone'`), filtered by `rarity` (a list) and `maxSkill` when given, or pinned with `id`; fish slots expose {fish.name} and {fish.id}. Goal `catch` = land `count` of `target` (a fish id) with a rod; `pool: true` = only catches from a fish pool count; target 'junk' = junk catches. These frames are offered by anglers (role 'angler'); until the server has a `fish` slot pool they simply never bind.",
  "rules": {
    "preferUndiscovered": "A vignette/fort/settlement slot picks a place the character has NOT discovered with weight x4 over discovered ones (PLAN §3.4 'prefer undiscovered places').",
    "maxOffered": 4,
    "refreshMinutes": 20,
    "repeatGapMinutes": 60,
    "perCharacter": true
  },
